# expect.stdout: 0\n
# expect.exit: 0
# expect.xfail: feature_coverage.py runs through bootstrap_general.sscript which does not yet wrap a `run CALL` in a retry loop when `useRetry CALL POLICY` attaches a policy. Direct semsc.py compilation works correctly (`python compiler/semsc.py THIS_FILE --emit-exe /tmp/x.exe && /tmp/x.exe` prints `0\n` because the retry loop runs the call 3 times until the counter walks from -3 to 0). Closing means teaching bootstrap_general to emit retry_top/body/inc/exit blocks around `run` when the call has a policy attached.
project UseRetryLoop
target console
runtime AgentRuntime 0.1
